  "result": "Excellent! All 286 tests pass. I've successfully added foreign currency support to the money module:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/money.js** - Added:\n   - `RATES` export: `{ EUR: 1, USD: 1.085, GBP: 0.8425 }` - units of that currency per euro\n   - `convert(cents, currency)` - Converts EUR cents to target currency:\n     - Returns `ok(amount in target currency's cents)` on success\n     - Returns `fail(UNKNOWN_CURRENCY)` for unknown currencies\n     - Uses banker's rounding to maintain precision\n   - `formatMoney(cents, currency)` - Formats amounts with proper currency symbols:\n     - EUR: `\u20ac` (e.g., \u20ac1,234.56)\n     - USD: `$` (e.g., $1,234.56)\n     - GBP: `\u00a3` (e.g., \u00a31,234.56)\n     - Includes thousands separators and 2 decimal places\n\n2. **src/errors.js** - Added:\n   - `UNKNOWN_CURRENCY` error code with message\n\n3. **test/money.test.js** - Comprehensive test coverage (31 tests):\n   - RATES object verification\n   - EUR to EUR conversion (identity)\n   - EUR to USD conversion (1000 EUR = $1,085.00)\n   - EUR to GBP conversion (1000 EUR = \u00a3842.50)\n   - Small amount conversions with proper rounding\n   - Unknown currency handling\n   - Negative amounts and zero amounts\n   - All three currencies formatted correctly\n   - Thousands separators\n   - Edge cases and fractional rounding\n\nThe implementation correctly handles currency conversion using banker's rounding, maintains cent-precision throughout calculations, and provides localized formatting for display.",
